# luna-decision-core environment file template. Copy it to .env.local (git-ignored) and fill in
# only the lines you need. Every line below is commented out, so this file sets nothing.
#
#   bash:        cp .env.example .env.local
#   PowerShell:  Copy-Item .env.example .env.local
#
# Lookup: .env.local, then .env, in the package folder (the luna-decision-core folder itself, not
# the folder you are working in), then in LUNA_CORE_HOME. A variable that is already set and not
# empty in the shell always wins. The first file that sets a variable wins. Only LUNA_* and
# OPENAI_* variables are read. Never commit a file that holds a real key.
#
# Put comments on their own lines: a value is everything after the "=" on that line.

# Luna calls are billed to this key. Heuristic mode needs no key at all.
# LUNA_API_KEY takes precedence over OPENAI_API_KEY when both are set.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# LUNA_API_KEY=

# Mode: auto (default; Luna, falling back to the rules), luna (strict; a Luna failure fails the
# decision), or heuristic (rules only; no network, no key).
# LUNA_CORE_MODE=auto

# Decisions API endpoint and model. Changing the URL sends the decision texts and the key there.
# LUNA_DECISION_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1/decisions
# LUNA_DECISION_MODEL=gpt-6-luna

# Per-call timeout in milliseconds (a positive integer). A timeout pauses Luna for 30 seconds.
# LUNA_DECISION_TIMEOUT_MS=4000

# Prompt cache mode for the shared rubric: explicit (default), implicit, or off.
# LUNA_CACHE=explicit

# Below this confidence Luna abstains and the rules decide. A number from 0 to 1.
# LUNA_MIN_CONFIDENCE=0.4

# Optional OpenAI organization and project, sent as headers with Luna calls.
# OPENAI_ORG_ID=
# OPENAI_PROJECT_ID=

# Home folder for memory.jsonl, decisions.jsonl and config.json. Default: ~/.luna-decision-core.
# Set it in the shell, not in an env file, so that the env files are found in the same place.
# LUNA_CORE_HOME=

# Path to a JSON config file. Relative paths resolve from the current folder.
# LUNA_CORE_CONFIG=
